44:57.538 --> 44:58.279
[SPEAKER_00]: He's not married.

44:58.619 --> 44:59.720
[SPEAKER_00]: So it could happen.

45:00.380 --> 45:07.104
[SPEAKER_00]: But really, if you think about it, you could be the next ruler of Monmurg.

45:07.124 --> 45:16.370
[SPEAKER_00]: So Jude is basically saying, you develop these people to think, someday, Paul Rivero may make me.

45:18.023 --> 45:29.490
[SPEAKER_00]: Paul Ribeiro may make the next Lord of the Dungeons or the head merchant of the trade district, something like that.

45:30.130 --> 45:34.693
[SPEAKER_00]: What he's trying to say to you is develop your own infrastructure.

45:35.153 --> 45:43.378
[SPEAKER_01]: Another way to look for these people, another way to look for these people, is they will be the ones that like, so the intelligent lieutenant

45:44.198 --> 45:44.739
[SPEAKER_01]: That's loyal.

45:45.299 --> 45:47.341
[SPEAKER_01]: That doesn't express bitterness or resentment.

45:47.522 --> 45:48.122
[SPEAKER_01]: Any lieutenant.

45:48.543 --> 46:02.017
[SPEAKER_01]: But let's say that like in the guard or a lieutenant below the captain of the watch or the gate, that you see in a meeting is providing valuable information to the captain and is slightly disregarded.

46:03.038 --> 46:07.499
[SPEAKER_01]: Not held in super high esteem, but he's there, and you can see... Or the sergeant.

46:07.519 --> 46:16.822
[SPEAKER_01]: Right, or the sergeant that does a tremendous amount of work, but he doesn't necessarily have his nose up like the captain's ass, because the captain just assumes... Because he's a captain.

46:17.002 --> 46:20.043
