46:20.483 --> 46:29.946
[SPEAKER_01]: But you, on observation, notice that he's actually a very capable man, capable himself of becoming captain.

46:32.188 --> 46:34.329
[SPEAKER_01]: So you look for the unappreciated underlings.

46:35.409 --> 46:36.029
[SPEAKER_01]: Still loyal.

46:38.710 --> 46:38.990
[SPEAKER_01]: I got it.

46:40.490 --> 46:42.691
[SPEAKER_01]: And don't just use money.

46:43.351 --> 46:51.073
[SPEAKER_01]: In this hard time... That'll get your poor civilian, but... Well, that and just...

46:51.093 --> 46:53.573
[SPEAKER_01]: They can also be smart enough to just bleed you dry.

46:54.213 --> 46:56.494
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I mean, their coffers do have limits.

46:57.523 --> 47:06.431
[SPEAKER_01]: So you don't want to be perceived to necessarily be buying their friendship because that also means that someone else can buy their enmity.

47:07.112 --> 47:11.896
[SPEAKER_01]: So you actually have to demonstrate, that's what I was saying, actual genuine care.

47:12.336 --> 47:23.907
[SPEAKER_01]: So for instance when I was talking about the bastards, if you're not full of shit and you're not lying to them and you would, because of their talents, see them

47:25.202 --> 47:31.069
